*** Keywords ***
TC__Cloud_PM_PIM_Alarms_Triggering
    [Arguments]  ${scfc_file_path}  ${rmod_sn_list}=@{EMPTY}  ${rmod_sn_count}=0  ${log_to_console}=True
    [Documentation]
    ...  Description:
    ...  [CASE LINK]: https://jiradc.ext.net.nokia.com/browse/FCA_ST_SISO-28307
    ...  Feature: CB010412-CR-E-B1 - SiSo parity feature,5GC001240 Adaption
    ...  Feature: 5GC001240-A-SyVe - PIM Cancellation - Faults Triggering
    ...  Test case for CB010412-CR-E-B1 SiSo parity feature (5GC001240 Adaption).
    ...
    ...  Test case verifies alarms related to PIM Cancellation.
    ...  Passive Intermodulation (PIM) is the unwanted signal (or signals) that is generated by
    ...  the non-linear mixing of two or more frequencies in a passive (or linear) device, such as a connector or cable.
    ...  If those signals fall on UL channels, receiver performance becomes degraded.
    ...  The PIM cancellation algorithm correlates the transmitted signal in the same antenna port with the received signal,
    ...  detects the intermodulation distortion components and removes them from the received signal.
    ...  The algorithm is cancelling only the first two orders of the effect - IM3 and IM5.
    ...  Once the algorithm sensitivity is manipulated to catch even thermal noise as PIM, one can trigger PIMC alarm
    ...  (even in a perfect RF environment) and perform this test correctly.
    ...  This functionality is provided with feature LTE2863 and parity feature 5GC001240.
    ...  The purpose of this test case is to verify alarms related to PIMC.
    ...
    ...  Step 1: Initial check PIM alarms triggering
    ...  a) No unexpected alarm is visible
    ...  b) vDU operation state is OnAir (operational_state=OnAir)
    ...  c) All cells are OnAir
    ...     Cells expected states: operational_state = enabled
    ...                            administrative_state = unlocked
    ...                            availability_status = on_line
    ...  Step 2: Enable PIM Cancellation feature
    ...  a) Check if radio module serial number is in configuration
    ...  b) Check if PIM Cancellation feature is enabled
    ...  c) Enable PIM Cancellation (actPimCancellation=true, pimCancellingEnabled=true)
    ...  Step 3: Generate Minor PIM Cancellation alarm
    ...  a) Setting PIM Cancellation alarm thresholds: minor=-180 and major=-30 (update parameter of delta plan)
    ...  b) Waiting for 1999 faults with Minor severity on impacted antennas
    ...  c) All cells are OnAir
    ...     Cells expected states: operational_state = enabled
    ...                            administrative_state = unlocked
    ...                            availability_status = on_line
    ...  d) No unexpected alarm is visible
    ...  Step 4: Reset radio module while Minor PIM Cancellation alarm is active
    ...  a) Radio module unit reset
    ...  b) Waiting for 1999 faults with Minor severity on impacted antennas
    ...  c) All cells are OnAir
    ...     Cells expected states: operational_state = enabled
    ...                            administrative_state = unlocked
    ...                            availability_status = on_line
    ...  Step 5: Generate Minor and Major PIM Cancellation alarm
    ...  a) Setting PIM Cancellation alarm thresholds: minor=-180 and major=-179 (update parameter of delta plan)
    ...  b) Waiting for 1999 faults with Minor severity on impacted antennas
    ...  c) Waiting for 2900 faults with Major severity on impacted antennas
    ...  d) Checking if all impacted cells has state "degraded"
    ...  e) No unexpected alarm is visible
    ...  Step 6: Cancel PIM Cancellation alarms
    ...  a) Setting PIM Cancellation alarm thresholds: minor=-31 and major=-30 (update parameter of delta plan)
    ...  b) Waiting for cancelling 1999 faults with Minor severity on impacted antennas
    ...  c) Waiting for cancelling 2900 faults with Major severity on impacted antennas
    ...  d) All cells are OnAir
    ...     Cells expected states: operational_state = enabled
    ...                            administrative_state = unlocked
    ...                            availability_status = on_line
    ...  e) Radio module should be online
    ...  f) No unexpected alarm is visible
    ...  Step 7: Disable PIM Cancellation feature
    ...  a) Disable PIM Cancellation (actPimCancellation=false, pimCancellingEnabled=false)
    ...  b) vDU operation state is OnAir (operational_state=OnAir)
    ...  c) All cells are OnAir
    ...     Cells expected states: operational_state = enabled
    ...                            administrative_state = unlocked
    ...                            availability_status = on_line
    ...  d) No unexpected alarms are visible
    ...
    ...  Arguments:
    ...  +========================+======+============================================================================+
    ...  | Argument               | Man. | Description                                                                |
    ...  +========================+======+============================================================================+
    ...  | scfc_file_path         | Yes  | Path to the vDU scfc file.                                                 |
    ...  +------------------------+------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | rmod_sn_list           |      | List of serial number of the tested radio modules.                         |
    ...  |                        |  No  | @{EMPTY} value means that no list was given,                               |
    ...  |                        |      | so all radio modules defined in the SCFC file will be used.                |
    ...  +------------------------+------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | rmod_sn_count          |  No  | Number of randomly selected radio modules serial numbers based on          |
    ...  |                        |      | the list obtained from the SCFC file.                                      |
    ...  +------------------------+------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | log_to_console         |  No  | Show or not the information on the console.                                |
    ...  +------------------------+------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...
    ...  Author: slawomir.jastrzebski@nokia.com
    ...  Maintainer: slawomir.jastrzebski@nokia.com

